      "narration": {
        "text": "Exchange rates state one currency in terms of another. Here one dollar buys seventy five pence. A British buyer paying four hundred dollars for sensors needs three hundred pounds, because four hundred times nought point seven five equals three hundred. Reverse it: a three hundred pound order costs an American buyer four hundred dollars. Cards animate both directions. Every purchase crosses the rate, so every price changes twice.",
