      "narration": {
        "text": "Now the dollar depreciates: one dollar buys sixty pence, so the pound appreciates. The same three hundred pound order now costs the American buyer five hundred dollars, because three hundred divided by nought point six is five hundred. British exports are dearer. Meanwhile a four hundred dollar American order costs a British buyer two hundred forty pounds, not three hundred, so imports are cheaper. Northstar gains on costs, but its sales slow.",
