        "text": "A tariff is a tax put on imported goods entering the country. Here a border gate adds a ten percent tariff to a four hundred dollar component. That is forty dollars, so the landed cost becomes four hundred forty dollars. At one dollar to seventy five pence, Northstar pays three hundred thirty pounds instead of three hundred. The gate closes on cheap inputs and opens for local rivals.",
