      "narration": {
        "text": "Free trade and protection each have two sides. Free trade gives Northstar cheaper inputs, wider markets and more choice. Because competition is strong, therefore prices fall, so consumers benefit. Yet domestic firms can be squeezed and jobs lost. Protection saves jobs and infant industries, but tariffs raise costs, quotas limit supply and other countries may retaliate. For an importing firm, the balance tilts toward free trade. If the pound appreciates, imports get cheaper anyway, so a tariff hurts less. If the dollar strengthens, protection may look kinder.",
        "words": 87,
        "wpm": 145.0
