      "narration": {
        "text": "Now apply it. One dollar buys seventy five pence. A British firm owes four hundred dollars to a supplier. Later the dollar depreciates to sixty pence. What does the bill become in pounds, and are its exports dearer or cheaper for American buyers? On screen, two currency cards flip and a border gate opens. Choose, then watch the arrows settle. Two hundred forty pounds is the new bill, so imports are cheaper. A three hundred pound export now costs five hundred dollars, so overseas buyers pay more.",
